{{{{{1<noinclude>|Ability data</noinclude>}}}|Savagery|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|champion     = Rengar
|skill        = Q
|icon         = Savagery.png
|blurb        = {{sbc|Active:}} {{ci|Rengar}} gains {{sti|{{as|'''bonus''' attack speed}}}} for his next two {{tip|basic attacks}}. His next basic attack deals {{as|'''bonus''' physical damage}} and will {{tip|critically strike}}, dealing increased damage based on his {{sti|{{as|critical strike chance}}}}.
|blurb4      = {{sbc|{{ai|Savagery 2|Rengar|Ferocity}} Bonus:}} ''Savagery's'' damage is modified and '''Rengar''' gains {{sti|{{as|'''bonus''' attack speed}}}} for a few seconds.
|description  = {{sbc|Active:}} '''Rengar''' gains {{sti|{{as|40% '''bonus''' attack speed}}}} on his next two {{tip|basic attacks}} {{tip|on-attack}} within 3 seconds.
|description2 = His first attack {{tip|on-hit}} is empowered to stab the target, having an {{tip|uncancellable windup}}, gaining {{sti|range|25 '''bonus''' range}}, and dealing {{as|'''additional''' physical damage|physical damage}}.
|leveling2     = {{st|Additional Physical Damage|{{ap|20 to 160}} {{as|(+ 5% AD)}}}}
|icon3        = Savagery 2.png
|description3 = {{sbc|Ferocity Bonus:}} ''Savagery's'' damage is modified to deal {{pp|35 to 140 for 8; 150 + (240-150)/9*(x-1) for 12|formula = 20 + 15 per level until level 8, then + 10 per level|color=physical damage}} {{as|(+ 20% AD)}} {{as|'''bonus''' physical damage}}. In addition to gaining another instance of the base attack speed on-cast, consuming the attack also grants {{as|{{pp|key=%|50 + (101-50)/17*(x-1) for 20}} '''bonus''' attack speed}} for 5 seconds.
|description4 = ''Savagery {{tip|basic attack reset|resets}} '''Rengar's''' basic attack timer.''
|cooldown     = {{ap|6 to 4}}
|cdstart      = post-effect
|targeting    = Auto
|affects      = Self
|cast time    = none
|damagetype   = Physical
|spelleffects = Special
|spellshield  = false
|parry        = True
|notes        = 
* Casting ''Savagery'' does not {{tip|break stealth}}.
* The bonus attack speed from the unempowered and empowered casts can stack with each other, if both are cast shortly one after another.
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* The empowered attack windup may still be manually cancelled when targeting [[jungle plants]] or {{tip|turret|structures}}. [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJu20W1fg_c] {{bug|2}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q|estimatedPatchOrigin=V8.4|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776287727|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* Different attack speeds may desync the animation from the hit. [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x84g8DhU3H4] {{bug|2}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q|estimatedPatchOrigin=V25.05|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776216366|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}<!--patch origin estimated based on slow and steady augment release-->
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* {{tip|Interrupt|Interrupting}} {{ais|I|Rengar}} leap will shortly after replace ''Savagery's'' own animation with a normal basic attack animation. [https://github.com/ArdaSenyurek/Rengar-Bugs/issues/109] {{bug|2}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q|estimatedPatchOrigin=V26.01|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776216366|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* If {{tip|energized}} kills the target before the attack hits, ''Savagery'' won't be consumed but it will still grant free {{as|Ferocity|buzzword3}}. [https://github.com/ArdaSenyurek/Rengar-Bugs/issues/54] {{bug|2|Appeared on V26.01}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q; Energized|estimatedPatchOrigin=V26.01|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776025385|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}
* ''Savagery's'' empowered attack is consumed against [[jungle plants]].
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* While the {{as|Ferocity|buzzword3}} timer is not running, if the attack {{tip|blind|misses}} or is {{tip|dodge|dodged}} it will grant a permanent {{as|Ferocity|buzzword3}} stack until the timer is triggered and refreshed. [https://github.com/ArdaSenyurek/Rengar-Bugs/issues/55] {{bug|2|Appeared on V26.01}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q; Blind; Dodge|estimatedPatchOrigin=V26.01|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776025385|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* The '''additional''' damage is tagged as {{tip|proc damage}}, {{tip|basic damage}}, and {{tip|spell damage}}, and applies other {{tip|on-hit}} effects as well as {{as|{{sti|life steal}}}} as normal.
** It is also part of a separate {{tip|cast instance}} - potentially allowing an extra stack of {{ii|Eclipse}} and {{ri|Electrocute}} (e.g while using {{ii|Black Cleaver}}). [https://github.com/ArdaSenyurek/Rengar-Bugs/issues/103] {{bug|2|Issue became visible on V26.03}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q; Cast Instance|estimatedPatchOrigin=V26.01|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776025385|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}
{{safesubst:unexpected|desc=
* The in-game extended tooltip incorrectly states that the '''additional''' damage is reduced against structures. [https://imgur.com/a/4e4dZiz] {{bug|2|This was supposed to be removed in V26.01}}|affectedEffects=Rengar Q|estimatedPatchOrigin=V26.01|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1776216366|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Rengar/Savagery
}}
<!--* While ''Savagery'' is active, using {{iis|Tiamat}} {{nie|Crescent}}, {{iis|Ravenous Hydra}} {{nie|Ravenous Crescent}}, {{iis|Profane Hydra}} {{nie|Heretical Cleave}}, or {{iis|Stridebreaker}} {{nie|Breaking Shockwave}} before ''Savagery's'' first attack will cause them to have no winddown animation.{{bug}}
** This is only cosmetic and bares no effect on gameplay.
* Attempting to cast {{iis|Tiamat}} {{nie|Crescent}}, {{iis|Ravenous Hydra}} {{nie|Ravenous Crescent}}, {{iis|Profane Hydra}} {{nie|Heretical Cleave}}, or {{iis|Stridebreaker}} {{nie|Breaking Shockwave}} during ''Savagery's'' first attack's [[Basic attack#Windup|attack windup]] will cause it to have no winddown animation.{{bug}}
** This is only cosmetic and bares no effect on gameplay.-->
}}

